4   dividends $2,960.15; net short-term loss (1,844.00)\nOther:         Amy sold handmade jewelry online, \"about $3k\" gross, no 1099 received. Receipts in shoebox.\n\nPART 5 -- DEDUCTIONS (Schedule A items)\nMortgage interest (Form 1098): Midland Prairie Mortgage Co., loan 7700218834             $14,208.39\nReal estate tax, DuPage County, PIN 07-22-304-019                         $11,940.22\nCharity:  Redeemed Life Assembly (weekly giving statement attached)               $6,240.00\n          Naperville Central Band Boosters                                     $350\nMedical:  Tobi's insulin pump and CGM supplies -- he has type 1 diabetes, dx 2021.\n          Out of pocket after insurance approx. $7,150. Paid from HSA? \"Some.\" (need Form 8889 detail)\n\nPART 6 -- CHILD CARE (Form 2441)\nProvider:  Little Sprouts Montessori, 1550 W. Ogden Ave., Naperville    EIN 84-3317206    Paid $4,875 (Folake, after-school)\nSitter:    Marguerite Dunleavy, SSN \"she won't give it to us\" -- paid $2,400 by Zelle to 630.555.0149\n\nPART 7 -- ESTIMATED PAYMENTS\nNone federal. Illinois: $600 on 6/16/25, $600 on 9/15/25.\n\nPART 8 -- QUESTIONS FOR YOUR PREPARER\n- \"Bayo got an IRS Letter 5071C in January asking him to verify his identity. Do we\n  ignore it? He did not file anything yet.\"\n- \"We paid Mrs. Dunleavy more than last year. Do we need to give her a form?\"\n- \"Compare 2024 2025 withholding -- why was our refund so much smaller?\"\n\nOFFICE USE: organizer complete? N -- missing HSA statement, 1099-B pages 3-6, mother's passport copy.\nAssigned: SY.   Target date: 3/20/2026.", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "480 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Adebayo T. Oyelaran", "Chiamaka Oyelaran", "Tobi Oyelaran", "Folake Oyelaran", "Abiodun Oyelaran", "Amy", "Folake", "Marguerite Dunleavy", "Bayo"], "companies": ["Lakeview Compounding Pharmacy, Inc.", "Fox Prairie School District 88", "Prairie State Bank & Trust", "Midland Prairie Mortgage Co.", "Harborstone Securities"